      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here is the **Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report** for your review:\n\n---\n\n# Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim, VP of Sales | Claire Fontaine, CFO\n**Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nQ3 2026 marks another strong quarter for Meridian Analytics. Across our 15-person team we closed 14 deals out of 22 opportunities, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The sales pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals in the pending stage. Customer support ticket volume held steady, with critical issues resolved same-day in all cases.\n\n---\n\n## Sales Performance\n\n- **Total closed revenue:** **$1,040,000**\n- **Top region:** South \u2014 **$468,000** in won deals\n- **Field sales team:** James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb \u2014 22 active opportunities\n- **Win rate:** **63.6%** (above the 55% company target)\n- **Pending deals:** ~$240,000 across 3 deals expected to close by end of September\n- **Product mix:** Meridian Insights Pro led closed revenue; Meridian DataBridge driving land-and-expand for Q4\n\n---\n\n## Key Highlights\n\n- **Top deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract with a Southern-region enterprise customer on September 5 (D019)\n- **Team headcount:** 15 employees across 5 departments \u2014 Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), Finance (2)\n- **Support SLA:** All critical-priority tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) resolved within 24 hours\n- **License utilisation:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) at **94% capacity** \u2014 procurement review scheduled for October\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Close the three pending deals (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target **$1.2M** in new ARR\n3. Resolve open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of quarterly customer success calls\n4. Conduct a license capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi to support Q4 roadmap\n\n---\n\nThe report has also been saved as a formatted Word document at `Q3_2026_Business_Report_Executive_Team.docx`. Let me know if you'd like to dive deeper into any section, or if you'd like me to pull up the supporting data (sales details, expenses, support tickets, etc.).",
